      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nFrom ReadMe : \"On CLOB fill, filled amounts are rounded down to the nearest lot. FOK fill orders should not revert if only the amount rounded off is left unfilled, and the user is not charged for the dust.\" [link](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/README.md?plain=1#L31)\n\nBut right now, code enforce this instruction only if amountIsBase is false. If it is true the FOK fill Orders will get revert.\n\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L817\n```solidity\n    function _matchIncomingOrder(\n        Book storage ds,\n        Order storage makerOrder,\n        Order memory takerOrder,\n        uint256 matchedPrice,\n        bool amountIsBase\n    ) internal returns (__MatchData__ memory matchData) {\n        uint256 matchedBase = makerOrder.amount;\n        uint256 lotSize = ds.settings().lotSizeInBase;\n\n        if (amountIsBase) {\n            // denominated in base\n=@1>            matchData.baseDelta = (matchedBase.min(takerOrder.amount) / lotSize) * lotSize;\n            matchData.quoteDelta = ds.getQuoteTokenAmount(matchedPrice, matchData.baseDelta); \n            //..while limitOrder sellmakerOrder got matched with max buyMakerOrder price , while filling Buy taker Order, matched with minimum makerOrder(sell) price\n=@2>            matchData.matchedAmount = matchData.baseDelta;\n        } else {\n            // denominated in quote\n            matchData.baseDelta =\n                (matchedBase.min(ds.getBaseTokenAmount(matchedPrice, takerOrder.amount)) / lotSize) * lotSize;\n            matchData.quoteDelta = ds.getQuoteTokenAmount(matchedPrice, matchData.baseDelta);\n            matchData.matchedAmount = matchData.baseDelta != matchedBase ? takerOrder.amount : matchData.quoteDelta; \n        }\n         ....\n    }\n```\n\nLets say for `price = 1 ether`, there is only 1 Buy Order of `size = 10 ether` in the order book.\nNow the incoming Fill Ask Order has been executed with the same price and `baseAmount = 10 ether - 9` and the `lotSize = 10` , `amountIsBase = true`\n\nthe execution reaches, [@1](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L819)  => `matchData.baseDelta =  10 ether - 10`\n\n[@2](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L821) => `matchData.matchedAmount = 10 ether - 10`\n\nFunction exits and reaches [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L797), \n\n`incomingOrder.amount = (10 ether - 9) - (10 ether - 10)  = 1` \n\nAnd it will exit this [loop](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L779) since there are no other matching Order. (Even if there is one more matching Order, the loop is exited from [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L795) in the next iteration since `currMatch.baseDelta =  (1 /10 )* 10 = 0` without updating incomingOrder.amount. So the `incomingOrder.amount stays 1` in this case too )\n\nSince the `1` is the remaining value that has been rounded off while dividing with the lotSize(10) , the transaction should not revert.\n\nBut, inside the _processFillAskOrder() , this [condition](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L469) checks `newOrder.amount > 0` and will revert with `FOKOrderNotFilled()` message.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n```diff\nfunction _processFillAskOrder(\n        Book storage ds,\n        address account,\n        Order memory newOrder,\n        PostFillOrderArgs memory args\n    ) private returns (PostFillOrderResult memory) {\n        (uint256 quoteReceived, uint256 baseSent) = _matchIncomingAsk(ds, newOrder, args.amountIsBase);\n\n        if (quoteReceived == 0 || baseSent == 0) revert ZeroCostTrade();\n+        uint256 lotSize = ds.settings().lotSizeInBase;\n+        newOrder.amount = args.amountIsBase ? newOrder.amount / lotSize :newOrder.amount ; //if amountInBase = false ,  the _matchIncomingOrder() logic took care of it already.\n        if (args.fillOrderType == FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL && newOrder.amount > 0) revert FOKOrderNotFilled();\n\n        // slither-disable-next-line reentrancy-events This external call is to the factory\n        uint256 takerFee = _settleIncomingOrder(ds, account, Side.SELL, quoteReceived, baseSent);\n\n        emit FillOrderProcessed(\n            CLOBEventNonce.inc(),\n            account,\n            newOrder.id.unwrap(),\n            quoteReceived.toInt256(),\n            -baseSent.toInt256(),\n            takerFee\n        );\n\n        return\n            PostFillOrderResult(account, newOrder.id.unwrap(), quoteReceived.toInt256(), -baseSent.toInt256(), takerFee);\n    }\n```\n\nchanging the _matchIncomingOrder() logic also works, but it will overlaps with postLimitOrder() executions and create issues while IMMEDIATE_OR_CANCEL limit orders are being created.In this case, the remaining incomingOrder.amount if its greater than MIN_MIN_LIMIT_ORDER_AMOUNT_BASE must be written to the OrderBook and shouldnt be roundedOff and discarded.",
      "proofOfConcept": "```solidity\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase} from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\nimport {Side} from \"contracts/clob/types/Order.sol\";\nimport {ICLOB} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOB.sol\";\n\n\ncontract PoC is PoCTestBase {\n\n    error FOKOrderNotFilled();\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        address maker = users[0];\n        address taker = users[1];\n        uint256 price = 1 ether;\n\n        \n        setupTokens(Side.SELL, maker, 100 ether, price, true); // credited 100e^18 quoteTokens token to maker\n        setupTokens(Side.BUY, taker, 100 ether, price, true); // credited 100e^18 baseTokens token to taker\n\n        //setting lotsize = 10 thorughout\n        vm.prank(address(clobManager));\n        clob.setLotSizeInBase(10);  \n\n        uint256 amountInBase1 = 1 ether;\n        ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory limitArgs = setupPostLimitOrderArgs(Side.SELL, maker, amountInBase1, price);\n\n        vm.prank(maker);\n        clob.postLimitOrder(maker, limitArgs);\n\n        //taker tries to fill amountInBase1 amount by FILL OR KILL order type.\n        uint256 amountInBase2 = 1 ether - 9;   \n\n        ICLOB.PostFillOrderArgs memory fillArgs =  setUpPostFillOrderArgs(taker, Side.BUY, amountInBase2, price, true); \n\n        vm.prank(taker);\n        vm.expectRevert(FOKOrderNotFilled.selector);\n        clob.postFillOrder(taker, fillArgs);  //will revert\n\n        //now lets try to fill with amountIsBase = false\n        uint256 amountInQuoteToken = clob.getQuoteTokenAmount(price,amountInBase2);\n        fillArgs =  setUpPostFillOrderArgs(taker, Side.BUY, amountInQuoteToken, price, false);  \n       \n        vm.prank(taker);\n        clob.postFillOrder(taker, fillArgs); //will not revert\n    \n    }\n\n    function setupPostLimitOrderArgs(Side side, address user, uint256 amountInBase, uint256 price)\n        public returns (ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory args)\n    {\n       \n        args = ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase: amountInBase,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            price: price,\n            cancelTimestamp: setupOrderExpiry,\n            side: side,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n        });\n       \n    }\n\n    function setUpPostFillOrderArgs(\n        address taker,\n        Side side,\n        uint256 amount,\n        uint256 price,\n        bool amountIsBase\n    ) internal returns (ICLOB.PostFillOrderArgs memory fillArgs) {\n\n        fillArgs = ICLOB.PostFillOrderArgs({\n            amount: amount,\n            priceLimit: price,\n            side: side,\n            amountIsBase: amountIsBase,\n            fillOrderType: ICLOB.FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL\n        });\n \n    }\n}\n```",
